WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-It's great to see you,
as always.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.567
I've missed you, pal.
-You too.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.734
-It's always good to see you,
man.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.133
Doesn't that feel good, huh?
That audience?

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.434
-No.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.501
-It doesn't.
It doesn't feel good.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:11.801
-I'm kidding.
It feels great.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:14.434
It's nice to see all you guys.
We've all been cooped up

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:15.834
in our house.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:18.601
-I know they just announced
this thing last week,

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:22.033
that you're going to play
Jerry Garcia in a movie

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.734
with Martin Scorsese directing.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.267
-Yes. Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.467
-I love it.
I think it's fantastic.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.834
How did it come about?
And --

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.667
-This is a cool story
that I'll tell,

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:35.033
if anyone's watching,
that needs to improve

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.567
their voice of self-doubt
in their heads.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.100
Okay?
-We're all listening.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.133
-So, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.901
I'm sure.
I do -- I suffer from it.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.434
So, COVID started.
I started my company,

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.567
Strong Baby Productions.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.467
Shout-out,
Strong Baby Productions.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.934
And we had just started
the company.

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.834
And I'm on Instagram.
COVID just started.

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.701
We're all stuck in our houses.
And I see this picture

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.567
of Jerry Garcia when he's young,
and I'm like,

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.234
"Wow.
Why has nobody done this?

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.067
Why hasn't anyone made a movie?
I could play Jerry Garcia."

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.868
And then, I spent
the next hour and a half, like,

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.434
talking myself out of it,

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.634
being like,
"Don't show anyone this.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.801
Don't say this.
You're gonna sound insane.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.267
You're not good enough.
You're not this.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.701
You're not that."

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:18.300
And, you know, "He's an icon,
and that's just a picture."

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.901
And I finally did the work
in my head to go,

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.901
"No, share it with
the people you work with."

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:27.801
So I sent it to my company
and to my manager, Rick, and --

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:31.334
and they were like,
"This is a great idea."

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.300
And then,
Rick manages Martin Scorsese.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.901
And we worked together
on "Wolf of Wall Street,"

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.834
and he said, "You know who would
love this is Martin Scorsese."

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:41.300
And my partner Matt and I
were like, "Yeah, for sure.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.467
That sounds great."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.200
Like, "Yeah, I'm sure you --
yeah.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.400
I bet he'll like it a lot."

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.868
And we're like,
"What is happening?"

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:50.200
And then, Marty said, yes,
he wanted to direct a movie

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.567
about the Grateful Dead
with me playing Jerry Garcia.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-So it goes from zero --

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:59.167
-It goes to, I shouldn't even
send this because I am not

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:02.167
valuable enough
to even express an idea

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.767
to having your hero
direct a movie

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.667
about your nother hero,
you know?

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.501
-Yeah.
-And so it's a beautiful story.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.100
-Actually, it's happening.
Oh, my goodness.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.634
-Yeah, so that's really cool,
yeah.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.300
-Buddy, I can't wait for this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.033
I'm so excited.
So they're writing it now?

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.868
-Yeah, Larry and Scott,
my favorite writers,

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.567
who were, like,
"People vs. Larry Flynt"

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.734
and "Ed Wood" and stuff,
they're writing it now.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.167
And -- And it's exciting.
Let's hope it works out.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.234
-I'm so psyched for you, man.
-Thank you.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:27.334
-You also directed this movie
I want to --

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:29.067
It's gonna be on Netflix.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.934
-You were telling me backstage.
Explain this.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.901
-I directed my second movie.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:36.367
It's a documentary, and it's
about therapy, in general.

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:41.334
And sort of getting therapy
out to the masses of people

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.334
whose families and cultures
stigmatize it

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.834
and who can't afford it.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.434
And it's through the prism of me
and my therapist --

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.701
my actual therapist.
So it's an insane idea.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:53.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's an insane movie.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:56.234
I'm pretty sure we deal
with a lot of how insane,

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:58.267
ethically, it is for a patient
to be making a movie

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.634
about their therapist with them.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:05.067
But, ultimately, the idea
is to explore how therapy

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.901
has helped me in my life
and give that

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:09.501
to as many people as possible
would be awesome.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:10.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love that.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.400
-Yeah.
-I also want to talk about

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.968
"Don't Look Up."
This is your new movie.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.200
-What's that now, sweetheart?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.367
"Don't Look --"

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:20.934
-"Don't Look Up" is the film
I'm in -- got it.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.701
Okay. Yes. Great.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:28.467
Wow, I must be rusty, dude.
'Cause --

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:29.901
-Whoa!
You get rusty?

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.868
-Yeah.
-What do you mean?

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.601
You felt rusty,
or you feel it now?

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:36.133
-I felt --
Let's slow it down.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.300
Let's slow the pace down.
-I was going --

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.901
I was going a bit too much.
-Not you.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:44.868
Is our connection weird?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:45.901
-No. That's --

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.634
-Like, has stuff changed
between us?

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:50.834
-No. Is it me? You're not
feeling the vibe here?

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:55.434
-I think I'm being
broken up with by the world.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.033
-What are you talking about?
[ Audience shouting ]

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.767
-Okay.
I love you guys.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:03.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.234
-Sorry.
-I -- You know...

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.234
I thought I was getting dumped
for a second.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:08.501
-Are you kidding me?
-Yeah.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:11.601
-Never in your life.
-Thank God. Okay.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.667
-We will never,
ever let you down.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.634
We'd never dump you.
-Thank you.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.834
-This should be your home.
Yeah, I'm gonna move in here.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:21.000
-You're welcome.
You're welcome to move here.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.367
-Thanks, guys.
I want to talk to you about

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.701
you new film.
-"Don't Look Up" --

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.667
awesome movie
directed by Adam McKay.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.667
Legend.
Love McKay, dude.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.868
-Adam McKay is a genius.
He's brilliant.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.868
I want to talk about it
in the next segment.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.501
But I want -- you brought
something with you

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:37.234
that you've been using on the --
-On the press tour.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.400
-On the press tour.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.767
Now I do kind of
know what this is.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:45.801
-Okay. So this is a really bad,
like, 8-year-old style,

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.901
old-school fart machine.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:51.334
It literally says,
"Fart Machine #2" on it, okay?

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:52.934
[ Laughter ]
-That's really funny.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:56.734
-And it's huge and absurd
and crazy.

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.767
This is what it sounds like.
-All right.

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:01.801
-This is how digital
and dumb it sounds, okay?

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.934
[ Fart sounds ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.567
Okay?
Like, funny for, like,

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:09.300
a 6-year-old maybe, right?
-Sure.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.133
-So did I a movie
with Julia Louis-Dreyfus,

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:13.067
and she's the coolest.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.033
And I was saying, "I'm going
to do press for this movie,

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:17.133
'Don't Look Up,'" with all these
huge movie stars in it,

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.000
like Leonardo DiCaprio
and Meryl Streep

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.801
and Jennifer Lawrence
and Tyler Perry,

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.000
et cetera, et cetera,
Rob Morgan.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.334
And I'm like,
"Wouldn't it be funny

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:27.100
if I'm with all these
fancy people and I have, like,

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:30.167
a really stupid
3-year-old fart machine, right?"

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:32.467
[ Laughter ]
And so Julia, being awesome,

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:35.133
gets me this
as a wrap gift, okay?

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:41.567
And so I've been working
with the machine for a few --

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.400
for a few days now.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.801
And we did this big,
fancy press conference,

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.734
and I did the fart machine
when someone was talking about

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:51.000
climate change, and I -- I...
[ Audience "Ohs" ]

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.601
...I hit the fart machine
like that, right?

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.300
My castmates did --
did not find it funny.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.033
Meryl Streep, being the
O.G. legend that she is,

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.033
did find it funny,
which is why I ride for her

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:04.701
any time, day or night.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.300
-That's right.
Meryl Streep.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.968
-Okay?
-Meryl Streep is what's up.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:09.868
-So then, Adam McKay,
the director of this giant,

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:12.534
fancy film, that is amazing,
by the way, he says,

00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:13.734
"Jonah --"
And he's a funny guy.

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.033
You've known McKay forever.
And he goes,

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.868
"Jonah, you're gonna
get a kick out of this.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:21.467
Netflix, who made the movie,
has, like, formally asked me

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:25.467
multiple times to ask you
formally to stop using

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:28.901
the fart machine
during press for the film."

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:30.667
Like, they don't find it funny,

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.033
and they don't find it
interesting."

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:36.234
And I found that hilarious,
right?

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:39.267
So, in that, they have now
formally asked me --

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.834
And people I work with
that I pay,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.400
they can't say,
"Stop using that,"

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.167
but they're like
"Hey, you know, we --

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:48.801
we find it funny, you know?

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:53.267
We -- We get the joke, you know?
But it's just Netflix.

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:54.667
You know, whatever."
-"The suits upstairs."

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:57.868
And so I just want to say
officially, I love you, Netflix.

00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:00.167
I love working with you.
I am a huge fan.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.968
I watch your streamer,
but no corporate entity

00:07:02.968 --> 00:07:05.701
will ever silence
my digital farts, mother [bleep]

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.701
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:17.701
♪♪

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.701
-More with Jonah Hill
when we come back!

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:20.901
Stick around, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:23.467
[ Fart sounds ]

